<title>USA: Nash Finch Co Q1 net, sales, revenues up.</title>
<headline>Nash Finch Co Q1 net, sales, revenues up.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>12 Weeks Ended</p>
<p>						   Mar 22,	  Mar 23,</p>
<p>						     1997		1996</p>
<p> Total sales and revenues		$ 947,832	$ 684,494</p>
<p> Earnings before income taxes		5,259	    4,699</p>
<p> Income taxes				    2,203	    1,903</p>
<p> Net earnings				    3,056	    2,796</p>
<p> Net earnings per share			  .27		.26</p>
<p> Average number of shares outstanding   11,276	   10,890</p>
<p>	     (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: Higher 1997 Q1 net due primarily to wholesale operations and reflects the contributions from acquisitions of T. J. Morris Co in July 1996, and Super Food Services Inc in November 1996; and revenue growth from a military division.</p>
<p>Sales to new independent wholesale accounts added since the first quarter of 1996 were also a contributing factor. Retail sales for the quarter were down due to the sale or closing of nine stores which was partially offset by the opening of two new stores since the end of the first quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
